  "policies": [
    {
      "id": "access",
      "title": "How access is decided",
      "text": "An active staff login, effective permissions, church/branch scope, subscription feature and any record ownership/state checks are separate requirements. Roles accumulate permissions. HQ widens location scope within grants; HQ does not grant every action. Church custom roles and overrides can differ from templates. A directory member is not a login role. Never infer a person's effective access solely from a role name. Page access does not prove write or record access."
    },
    {
      "id": "scope",
      "title": "Branch, HQ and leadership scope",
      "text": "Data always belongs to the signed-in church. Branch users are scoped to their branch; HQ users may see multiple branches only where authorized. Department heads and cell leaders can be restricted to assigned groups. The assistant does not inspect records, group assignments, selected filters or pending statuses. These specific checks are unverified; do not assert why a particular record is unavailable. Contact the church administrator to review assignments."
    },
    {
      "id": "reviews",
      "title": "Forms and reviewing responses",
      "text": "Forms use forms:list:read for the collection, forms:submissions:read for responses and forms:submissions:update for review. Only pending responses may be approved/rejected. Select visible responses, choose Approve selected or Reject selected, confirm the batch and supply a rejection reason when rejecting. Successful reviews clear from selection; failed ones remain for retry. Reading a form does not grant submission review. Public token forms do not require a login; they still follow server availability, deduplication and capacity checks."
    },
    {
      "id": "tables",
      "title": "Table navigation and display controls",
      "text": "The first two record columns stay visible during horizontal scrolling. The separating shadow appears only after scrolling away from the start. Table view separately changes row spacing and column width. Compact text uses ellipses; headers and numeric/currency widths retain size. Column actions selects several columns to show, hide, compact or expand. Fixed identifiers cannot be hidden. Export-enabled collections can export selected visible rows using visible columns. Module-owned bulk actions retain their own permissions. These settings do not change records."
    },
    {
      "id": "plans",
      "title": "Plans, permissions and historical access",
      "text": "Essentials supports 100 members, 2 staff accounts and 1 location, including giving categories, cash/bank and online giving, downloadable receipts, basic giving totals and administrator payment-provider setup. Email communication starts on Community; SMS, WhatsApp and advanced analytics start on Network. Community supports 300 members, 5 staff and 1 location. Network supports 1500 members, 15 staff and 3 locations. Enterprise has agreed limits. USD base monthly prices are $10/$20/$40, annual $108/$216/$432. Currency conversions are server-quoted and rounded up. Never calculate a payable amount yourself. Feature eligibility does not grant staff permission. Module reads, writes, exports and offline access require a suitable active plan, independently of staff roles. Records are retained after a downgrade and become accessible when the church has an eligible plan again. Exact current usage is not read by this assistant."
    },
    {
      "id": "admins",
      "title": "Administrator-only surfaces",
      "text": "Analytics, provider integrations, ChurchOS billing and Tawk live chat are restricted to church_admin/super_admin with the applicable grants. HQ status by itself does not make a user an administrator. The Help Centre is public. Church administrators assign staff access. Ask ChurchOS product guidance is available to active staff and is separate from human support chat."
    },
    {
      "id": "attendance",
      "title": "Attendance totals and individual check-ins",
      "text": "Services, events, department meetings and cell meetings distinguish individual named check-ins from overall headcount totals. General attendance requires total, with optional adult/children and male/female subtotals. Do not add named check-ins to headcount totals to calculate a larger attendance number. Read, create and update headcounts are separately permission gated. Roster selections may span searches; saves are bounded batches and partial failures retain unsaved selections."
    },
    {
      "id": "giving",
      "title": "Giving and financial visibility",
      "text": "Giving dashboard aggregate access is separate from transaction read/write access. Recording giving uses the selected branch, member, category and relevant service where authorized. Cell-group meeting giving is a combined meeting total rather than individual member gifts. Group leaders are checked against their assigned group. Recurring giving and payment processing require their own permissions/provider configuration. The assistant cannot read gifts, donor details or payment histories."
    },
    {
      "id": "providers",
      "title": "Messaging, payments and support",
      "text": "Church email, SMS, WhatsApp, live calls and giving payment processing require the church's configured, enabled provider accounts. Platform subscriptions use organization gateways separately. There is no fallback from a church's missing credentials to platform provider keys. Provider usage charges are separate from ChurchOS subscriptions. Support uses the default Tawk floating chat for active administrators; ticketing has been removed. The assistant cannot send messages, create tickets, change integrations or contact support on a user's behalf."
    },
    {
      "id": "offline",
      "title": "Offline workspace and recovery",
      "text": "Offline workspace access requires offline:read and previously prepared data. Offline editing supports only its documented workflows and sync checks; a successful local queue entry does not guarantee server acceptance. Reconnect and review sync results. Ask ChurchOS needs a connection; it does not read offline records. Account recovery and MFA use the normal sign-in screens. Never ask users to paste passwords, recovery codes or tokens."
    },
    {
      "id": "limits",
      "title": "What Ask ChurchOS can verify",
      "text": "This version provides product explanations, route navigation and current signed-in access summaries. It cannot create/edit/delete records, alter permissions, retrieve church business records, inspect screen text/DOM, see uploaded files or send email/chat. It sees only the user's typed question, bounded previous user questions and a normalized page template. Unsure answers must say what is missing and point to a guide or church administrator. Do not claim full or perfect knowledge."
    }
  ],
